    "rawResponses": {
      "classes": "1: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a bank.\n2: MATCH 11 -- Organisational Unit is the same concept.\n3: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes an IT operations team.\n4: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a service desk.\n5: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a network operations centre.\n6: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a security operations centre.\n7: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes an application owner.\n8: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a technical owner.\n9: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a business owner.\n10: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a business process.\n11: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a service level objective.\n12: NO MATCH -- Infrastructure is broader than an infrastructure component.\n13: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a server.\n14: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a virtual machine.\n15: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a container platform.\n16: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a cloud service.\n17: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a network device.\n18: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a network segment.\n19: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes an endpoint.\n20: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a storage system.\n21: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a data centre.\n22: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a site.\n23: NO MATCH -- A recovery environment is more specific than an environment.\n24: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a data asset.\n25: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a monitoring tool.\n26: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a monitoring rule.\n27: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a metric.\n28: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a log source.\n29: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a security event.\n30: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a major incident.\n31: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a cybersecurity incident.\n32: NO MATCH -- A problem record documents a problem; it is not the problem.\n33: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes an emergency change.\n34: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a release.\n35: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a business continuity plan.\n36: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a disaster recovery test.",
      "relationships": "1: NO MATCH -- Routing an incident is not the same as assigning it to a group.\n2: NO MATCH -- No candidate describes an engineer’s group membership.\n3: NO MATCH -- No candidate describes the commander’s team membership.\n4: MATCH 5 -- An IT service owned by a service owner expresses ownership.\n5: NO MATCH -- No candidate describes vendor support for an application.\n6: MATCH 15 -- Addressing a notification to a regulator means sending it to that regulator.\n7: NO MATCH -- No candidate describes stakeholder interest in a business service.\n8: MATCH 4 -- An IT service supporting a business service expresses the reverse dependency.\n9: NO MATCH -- No candidate describes an exposed integration interface.\n10: NO MATCH -- A plan applying to a service does not necessarily recover it.\n11: NO MATCH -- No candidate describes a recovery plan using a backup set.\n12: NO MATCH -- No candidate identifies where an event is observed.\n13: NO MATCH -- No candidate relates an event to an IT service.\n14: NO MATCH -- Arising from an event describes origin, not indication.\n15: NO MATCH -- No candidate describes an alert concerning an IT service.\n16: NO MATCH -- No candidate describes an alert concerning a configuration item.\n17: NO MATCH -- Linking an alert to an incident does not mean it opens one.\n18: NO MATCH -- Linking an event to an incident does not establish correlation from it.\n19: NO MATCH -- No candidate describes an incident’s impact on a business service.\n20: NO MATCH -- Assignment to an engineer does not establish handling by that engineer.\n21: NO MATCH -- No candidate describes handling an incident with a runbook.\n22: NO MATCH -- Preserving evidence differs from evidence documenting an incident.\n23: NO MATCH -- No candidate describes notifying a stakeholder.\n24: NO MATCH -- No candidate describes escalation to a vendor.\n25: NO MATCH -- No candidate connects incident recovery to a recovery plan.\n26: MATCH 10 -- An incident’s materia